module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.AffineChart
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityIII.BlowupTwistDownAnnihilation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TensorSectionNonvanishing.ProjTwistLeftSlotScalar
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Glueing.OModuleMapGluing

/-!
# `ℱ(q) ⟶ p^*K(q) ⟶ p^*K(q - c)` vanishes, and the dotted arrow of [Stacks, Tag 0GAA]

Let `A` be a commutative ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal and `p : X ⟶ Spec(A)` the blowup of `Spec(A)`
in `I`. `BitUniformityIII/BlowupTwistDownAnnihilation.lean` proves that the inclusion of
`ℱ(q) = ker(p^*K(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q))`, followed by twisting down to `q - c` and then by multiplication by
`(b⁽¹⁾)^c`, is zero for every `b ∈ I` and every integer `q`. This file drops the trailing factor
and draws the consequence.

## How the factor is dropped

The three inputs are all available, and none of them is [Stacks, Tag 0GA9]:

* multiplication by `(b⁽¹⁾)^c` is **bijective on the sections over every open inside
  `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`**. This is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistRestriction.bijective_twistSheafScalarMap_pow_app`, at the
  **left** tensor slot: that statement is about `ℱ ⊗ 𝒪(n)` and the geometric factor
  `N ↦ 𝒪_X(q) ⊗ p^*Ñ` carries the twist on the left, so the braiding of
  `TensorSectionNonvanishing/ProjTwistLeftSlotScalar.lean` is what makes it applicable;
* the opens `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`, `b ∈ I`, **cover** `Proj` of the Rees algebra —
  `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_basicOpen_reesDegOne_eq_top`, the Rees algebra being generated by its
  degree-one part;
* a morphism of presheaves of `𝒪`-modules into a **sheaf** is determined by its restrictions to
  a covering, with no compatibility hypothesis: `TopCat.Sheaf.eq_hom_of_restrict`. Taking the
  local morphisms to be `0` is "vanishes on a cover implies zero", so the gluing needs nothing
  constructed.

Injectivity alone is used, not bijectivity; the surjective half of that statement is not
needed here.

## The dotted arrow

With the vanishing, the dotted arrow of the diagram in the Stacks proof of clause (3) of
[Stacks, Tag 0GAA] exists for formal reasons and needs no further geometry. The second short
exact sequence `0 → ℱ(q) → p^*K(q) → 𝒢(q) → 0`
(`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.shortExact_twistedPullbackKernelSequence`) exhibits
`p^*K(q) ↠ 𝒢(q)` as the cokernel of the inclusion of `ℱ(q)`, so a morphism out of `p^*K(q)`
killing `ℱ(q)` descends to `𝒢(q)`; the morphism is the twisting-down map to `p^*K(q - c)` and
the vanishing is exactly the hypothesis `CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.Exact.desc` asks for. That
the descent **factors** `𝒢(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q - c)` is then one cancellation of the epimorphism against
`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.toCycles_naturality`.

## The two fields, and the two that are still missing

`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.blowupDotted` and `…kernelToImage_blowupDotted` are stated
at the declared types of the fields `dotted` and `kernelToImage_dotted` of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.TwistedModuleSituation`, read at the `ModuleSituation` the
blowup supplies. That passage turned out to cost nothing: the fields of
`…blowupModuleSituationOf` are `.hom` of the blowup's own `blowupHmodMap`, and
`ANCPresentation.resShortComplex_X₁` identifies the first term of the chosen presentation with
the `A`-module underlying `ANCPresentation.kernelANC` by `rfl`, so no transport occurs.

**No `TwistedModuleSituation` is constructed here, and none can be yet.** Its remaining two
fields are `secM` and `secM_freeSections`, the canonical maps `I^qM ⟶ H⁰(X, p^*M(q))` and their
compatibility with the chosen presentation; nothing in the tree constructs them, and they are a
separate development, as are the three fields `ev`, `ev_Htr` and `ev_secM` of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.DualSituation`. The five fields of
`BitUniformityIII/BlowupTwistDownCohomology.lean` are also still stated as morphisms of
`CategoryTheory.ModuleCat` rather than at the field types; the two below show that step is
routine, but it has not been carried out for them.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.twistDownDotted`: **the dotted arrow**
  `𝒢(q) ⟶ p^*K(q - c)` of sheaves of modules, from an arbitrary annihilation hypothesis.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.dottedOfPresentation`: the same at a chosen presentation
  of an `(A, n, c)`-module, where [Stacks, Tag 0GA8] supplies that hypothesis, so that the
  construction is unconditional.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.blowupDotted`: **the field `dotted`** of
  `TwistedModuleSituation`, at the blowup's `ModuleSituation`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.kernelι_comp_twistDown_eq_zero` and
  `…_of_mem`: **the vanishing** `ℱ(q) ⟶ p^*K(q) ⟶ p^*K(q - c) = 0`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.twistDownDotted_comp_toCycles` and
  `…dottedOfPresentation_comp_toCycles`: the dotted arrow factors `𝒢(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q - c)`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.blowupHmodMap_dottedOfPresentation_comp_toCycles`: that
  factorisation after `Hⁱ(X, -)`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.kernelToImage_blowupDotted`: **the field
  `kernelToImage_dotted`**, at the blowup's `ModuleSituation`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GAA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GAA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00AN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00AN)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections (twistScalarSheafMap)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistLeftSlot (bijective_geometricFactorFormulaMap_app
  bijective_tensorSheafMap_twistScalarSheafMap_pow_app)

universe u v₁ u₁

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII

attribute [local instance] modulesMonoidal modulesMonoidal' modulesEnoughInjectives
attribute [local instance] sheafSectionsPreservesFiniteLimits secFPreservesFiniteLimits
attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose
attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top

/-- The underlying morphism of presheaves of modules of the zero morphism of sheaves of modules
is the zero morphism. The `AddCommGroup` structure on the morphisms is transported along
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.fullyFaithfulForget`, so this is definitional; it is named only
because the simp set does not know it. -/
theorem zero_val {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}} {M P : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} R} :
    (0 : M ⟶ P).val = 0 := rfl

/-- **A morphism whose composite with a morphism injective on the sections over an object is
zero vanishes on those sections.** Nothing about sheaves is used: the composite's value on a
section is the second morphism applied to the first's, and the second is injective. -/
theorem val_app_eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C]
    {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
    {M N P : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} R} (ψ : M ⟶ N) (χ : N ⟶ P) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (hinj : Function.Injective (χ.val.app U)) (h : ψ ≫ χ = 0) :
    ψ.val.app U = 0 := by
  refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun x => hinj ?_)
  have hx := congrArg (fun z : M ⟶ P => z.val.app U x) h
  simpa [zero_val] using hx

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)

/-- **Multiplication by `(b⁽¹⁾)^c` is bijective on the sections over every open inside
`D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`, inside the geometric factor `N ↦ 𝒪_X(q) ⊗ p^*Ñ`.**

The twisting sheaf is the **left** tensor factor there, while the cited invertibility is stated
for the right one; the transport is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistLeftSlot.bijective_tensorSheafMap_twistScalarSheafMap_pow_app`,
and the identification of the geometric factor's action on its fixed factor with a left-slot
tensor map is `…bijective_geometricFactorFormulaMap_app`. The degree of `b⁽¹⁾` is `1`, so the
twist degrees of the cited statement — the products `m * d`, `n * d` and `j * d` — are matched
by `mul_one`, which is what its `subst`-generalised form is for. -/
theorem bijective_twistedPullbackTwistScalar_app (c : ℕ) (q' q : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q)
    {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I) (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) {W : (blowupScheme I).Opens}
    (hW : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen (Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading I) (Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne I hb)) :
    Function.Bijective
      (((twistedPullbackTwistScalar I c q' q hq
          ⟨(Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ^ c,
            Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOnePow_mem_reesGrading I hb c⟩).app N).val.app (op W)) :=
  bijective_geometricFactorFormulaMap_app A (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpOver I)
    (twistScalarSheafMap (Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading I) c q' q hq
      ⟨(Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne I hb : reesAlgebra I) ^ c,
        Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOnePow_mem_reesGrading I hb c⟩)
    N (op W) fun M =>
    bijective_tensorSheafMap_twistScalarSheafMap_pow_app (Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading I)
      (Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb) c q' q (mul_one c).symm
      (mul_one q').symm (mul_one q).symm
      (Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOnePow_mem_reesGrading I hb c) (by omega) hq M hW

variable {S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)} {c : ℕ}

/-- **The twisted-down map out of `ℱ(q)` vanishes on the sections over every open inside
`D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`.** Composing it with multiplication by `(b⁽¹⁾)^c` is zero, by
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.kernelι_comp_twistDown_comp_twistScalar_eq_zero`, and that
multiplication is injective on those sections. -/
theorem kernelι_comp_twistDown_val_app_eq_zero (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q)
    (hle : q' ≤ q) {b : A} (hb : b ∈ I)
    (hzero :
      letI : Linear A (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (blowupScheme I).ringCatSheaf) :=
        Stacks.Blowup.blowUpModulesLinear I
      (b ^ c) • 𝟙 (twistedPullbackSupported I q (S := S)) = 0)
    {W : (blowupScheme I).Opens}
    (hW : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen (Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading I) (Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne I hb)) :
    (kernel.ι (S.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q)).toCycles ≫
        (twistedPullbackTwistDown I q q' hle).app S.X₁).val.app (op W) = 0 :=
  val_app_eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero _ _ _
    (bijective_twistedPullbackTwistScalar_app I c q' q hq hb S.X₁ hW).1
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).trans
      (kernelι_comp_twistDown_comp_twistScalar_eq_zero I q q' hq hle hb hzero))

/-- **The twisted-down map out of `ℱ(q)` is zero.** The inclusion of
`ℱ(q) = ker(p^*K(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q))` followed by twisting down from `q` to `q - c` is the zero morphism,
as soon as `b^c` annihilates `ℱ(q)` for every `b ∈ I`.

It vanishes on each `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)` by `kernelι_comp_twistDown_val_app_eq_zero`, those opens cover
`Proj` of the Rees algebra by `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_basicOpen_reesDegOne_eq_top`, and a morphism of
presheaves of `𝒪`-modules into a sheaf is determined by its restrictions to a covering
(`TopCat.Sheaf.eq_hom_of_restrict`), with the local morphisms taken to be `0`. -/
theorem kernelι_comp_twistDown_eq_zero (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q) (hle : q' ≤ q)
    (hzero :
      letI : Linear A (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (blowupScheme I).ringCatSheaf) :=
        Stacks.Blowup.blowUpModulesLinear I
      ∀ b ∈ I, (b ^ c) • 𝟙 (twistedPullbackSupported I q (S := S)) = 0) :
    kernel.ι (S.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q)).toCycles ≫
        (twistedPullbackTwistDown I q q' hle).app S.X₁ = 0 := by
  refine _root_.SheafOfModules.hom_ext (TopCat.Sheaf.eq_hom_of_restrict
    (U := fun r : I => Proj.basicOpen (Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading I)
      (Stacks.Blowup.reesDegOne I r.2))
    (Stacks.Blowup.iSup_basicOpen_reesDegOne_eq_top I)
    ((twistedPullbackFunctor I q').obj S.X₁).isSheaf (fun _ _ _ => 0) (fun r V hV => ?_)
    (fun _ _ _ => rfl))
  exact kernelι_comp_twistDown_val_app_eq_zero I q q' hq hle r.2 (hzero r r.2) hV

/-- **The same at a chosen presentation of an `(A, n, c)`-module**, where the annihilation
hypothesis is [Stacks, Tag 0GA8] on this blowup,
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.smul_twistedPullbackSupported_eq_zero`, applied to
`b^c ∈ I^c` for each `b ∈ I`. So the vanishing is unconditional there. -/
theorem kernelι_comp_twistDown_eq_zero_of_mem {n : ℕ} {M : ANCModule I n c}
    (P : ANCPresentation I n c M) (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q) (hle : q' ≤ q) :
    kernel.ι (P.resShortComplex.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q)).toCycles ≫
        (twistedPullbackTwistDown I q q' hle).app P.resShortComplex.X₁ = 0 :=
  kernelι_comp_twistDown_eq_zero I q q' hq hle fun _ hb =>
    smul_twistedPullbackSupported_eq_zero P q (Ideal.pow_mem_pow hb c)

/-! ### The dotted arrow -/

/-- **The dotted arrow `𝒢(q) ⟶ p^*K(q - c)`** of the diagram in the Stacks proof of clause (3)
of [Stacks, Tag 0GAA].

`p^*K(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q)` is the cokernel of the inclusion of `ℱ(q)`, the second short exact sequence
being short exact, so the twisting-down map `p^*K(q) ⟶ p^*K(q - c)` descends along it as soon as
it kills `ℱ(q)` — which is `kernelι_comp_twistDown_eq_zero`. The descent is
`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.Exact.desc`, which asks for exactly that hypothesis. -/
def twistDownDotted (hS : S.ShortExact) (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q) (hle : q' ≤ q)
    (hzero :
      letI : Linear A (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (blowupScheme I).ringCatSheaf) :=
        Stacks.Blowup.blowUpModulesLinear I
      ∀ b ∈ I, (b ^ c) • 𝟙 (twistedPullbackSupported I q (S := S)) = 0) :
    twistedPullbackImage I q (S := S) ⟶ (twistedPullbackFunctor I q').obj S.X₁ :=
  have := (shortExact_twistedPullbackKernelSequence I q hS).epi_g
  (shortExact_twistedPullbackKernelSequence I q hS).exact.desc
    ((twistedPullbackTwistDown I q q' hle).app S.X₁)
    (kernelι_comp_twistDown_eq_zero I q q' hq hle hzero)

/-- The dotted arrow is a descent of the twisted-down map along `p^*K(q) ↠ 𝒢(q)`. -/
theorem toCycles_comp_twistDownDotted (hS : S.ShortExact) (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q)
    (hle : q' ≤ q)
    (hzero :
      letI : Linear A (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (blowupScheme I).ringCatSheaf) :=
        Stacks.Blowup.blowUpModulesLinear I
      ∀ b ∈ I, (b ^ c) • 𝟙 (twistedPullbackSupported I q (S := S)) = 0) :
    (S.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q)).toCycles ≫ twistDownDotted I hS q q' hq hle hzero =
      (twistedPullbackTwistDown I q q' hle).app S.X₁ :=
  have := (shortExact_twistedPullbackKernelSequence I q hS).epi_g
  (shortExact_twistedPullbackKernelSequence I q hS).exact.g_desc
    ((twistedPullbackTwistDown I q q' hle).app S.X₁)
    (kernelι_comp_twistDown_eq_zero I q q' hq hle hzero)

/-- **The dotted arrow factors `𝒢(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q - c)` through `p^*K(q - c)`.**

Both sides become equal after precomposition with the epimorphism `p^*K(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q)`: on the left
by the defining property of the descent followed by
`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.toCycles_naturality`, on the right by that naturality alone. -/
theorem twistDownDotted_comp_toCycles (hS : S.ShortExact) (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q)
    (hle : q' ≤ q)
    (hzero :
      letI : Linear A (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (blowupScheme I).ringCatSheaf) :=
        Stacks.Blowup.blowUpModulesLinear I
      ∀ b ∈ I, (b ^ c) • 𝟙 (twistedPullbackSupported I q (S := S)) = 0) :
    twistDownDotted I hS q q' hq hle hzero ≫
        (S.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q')).toCycles =
      twistDownCyclesMap I q q' hle (S := S) := by
  have := (shortExact_twistedPullbackKernelSequence I q hS).epi_g
  refine (cancel_epi (S.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q)).toCycles).1 ?_
  rw [← Category.assoc, toCycles_comp_twistDownDotted I hS q q' hq hle hzero]
  exact (ShortComplex.toCycles_naturality (twistDownShortComplexMap I q q' hle (S := S))).symm

/-- **The factorisation, pushed through `Hⁱ(X, -)`.** `Hⁱ(X, -)` is a functor, so this is
`twistDownDotted_comp_toCycles` under `CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp`; the rewrite under
`blowupHmodMap` is `blowupHmodMap_congr`, whose motive check is what a `rw` on a morphism of
sheaves of modules fails. -/
theorem blowupHmodMap_twistDownDotted_comp_toCycles (hS : S.ShortExact) (i : ℕ) (q q' : ℤ)
    (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q) (hle : q' ≤ q)
    (hzero :
      letI : Linear A (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (blowupScheme I).ringCatSheaf) :=
        Stacks.Blowup.blowUpModulesLinear I
      ∀ b ∈ I, (b ^ c) • 𝟙 (twistedPullbackSupported I q (S := S)) = 0) :
    blowupHmodMap I i (twistDownDotted I hS q q' hq hle hzero) ≫
        blowupHmodMap I i (S.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q')).toCycles =
      blowupHGtr I i q q' hle (S := S) :=
  (((blowupΓmod I).rightDerived i).map_comp _ _).symm.trans
    (blowupHmodMap_congr I i (twistDownDotted_comp_toCycles I hS q q' hq hle hzero))

/-! ### The dotted arrow at a chosen presentation -/

/-- **The dotted arrow at a chosen presentation of an `(A, n, c)`-module**, where the
annihilation hypothesis is [Stacks, Tag 0GA8] on this blowup. -/
def dottedOfPresentation {n : ℕ} {M : ANCModule I n c} (P : ANCPresentation I n c M)
    (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q) (hle : q' ≤ q) :
    twistedPullbackImage I q (S := P.resShortComplex) ⟶
      (twistedPullbackFunctor I q').obj P.resShortComplex.X₁ :=
  twistDownDotted I P.shortExact_resShortComplex q q' hq hle fun _ hb =>
    smul_twistedPullbackSupported_eq_zero P q (Ideal.pow_mem_pow hb c)

/-- **The dotted arrow does factor `𝒢(q) ⟶ 𝒢(q - c)` through `p^*K(q - c)`**, at a chosen
presentation. -/
theorem dottedOfPresentation_comp_toCycles {n : ℕ} {M : ANCModule I n c}
    (P : ANCPresentation I n c M) (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q) (hle : q' ≤ q) :
    dottedOfPresentation I P q q' hq hle ≫
        (P.resShortComplex.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q')).toCycles =
      twistDownCyclesMap I q q' hle (S := P.resShortComplex) :=
  twistDownDotted_comp_toCycles I P.shortExact_resShortComplex q q' hq hle _

/-- **The `Hⁱ(X, -)` form, which is the content of the field `kernelToImage_dotted`**: the
composite `Hⁱ(X, 𝒢(q)) ⟶ Hⁱ(X, p^*K(q - c)) ⟶ Hⁱ(X, 𝒢(q - c))` is `HGtr`. -/
theorem blowupHmodMap_dottedOfPresentation_comp_toCycles {n : ℕ} {M : ANCModule I n c}
    (P : ANCPresentation I n c M) (i : ℕ) (q q' : ℤ) (hq : (c : ℤ) + q' = q) (hle : q' ≤ q) :
    blowupHmodMap I i (dottedOfPresentation I P q q' hq hle) ≫
        blowupHmodMap I i (P.resShortComplex.map (twistedPullbackFunctor I q')).toCycles =
      blowupHGtr I i q q' hle (S := P.resShortComplex) :=
  blowupHmodMap_twistDownDotted_comp_toCycles I P.shortExact_resShortComplex i q q' hq hle _

/-! ### The two fields of `TwistedModuleSituation`, at the blowup's `ModuleSituation` -/

section Fields

variable [IsNoetherianRing A]

/-- **The field `dotted` of `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.TwistedModuleSituation`, on the
blowup**: the `A`-linear map `Hⁱ(X, 𝒢(q)) →ₗ[A] Hⁱ(X, p^*K(q - c))`.

The declared type is the field's, at the `ModuleSituation` the blowup supplies
(`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.blowupModuleSituationOf`), and it typechecks without a
transport: `H`, `HG` and `pres` there are the blowup's own `blowupHmod` at
`twistedPullbackImage` and at the twisted pullback of the first term of the chosen presentation,
and `CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.resShortComplex_X₁` identifies that term with the `A`-module
underlying `ANCPresentation.kernelANC` by `rfl`. -/
def blowupDotted (q₀ : ℕ) (h : IsBaseThreshold I q₀) (n c : ℕ) (hcn : c ≤ n)
    (M : ANCModule I n c) (i : ℕ) (q : ℤ) :
    (blowupModuleSituationOf I q₀ h n c hcn).HG M i q →ₗ[A]
      (blowupModuleSituationOf I q₀ h n c hcn).H
        ((blowupModuleSituationOf I q₀ h n c hcn).pres M).kernelANC i (q - c) :=
  (blowupHmodMap I i
    (dottedOfPresentation I (blowupANCPres I n c M) q (q - (c : ℤ)) (by ring) (by omega))).hom

/-- **The field `kernelToImage_dotted` of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.TwistedModuleSituation`, on the blowup**: the dotted arrow
does factor `Hⁱ(X, 𝒢(q)) ⟶ Hⁱ(X, 𝒢(q - c))` through `Hⁱ(X, p^*K(q - c))`.

This is `blowupHmodMap_dottedOfPresentation_comp_toCycles` read on an element; the field `HGtr`
of `TwistedModuleSituation` is `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.blowupHGtr`, as
`BitUniformityIII/BlowupTwistDownCohomology.lean` records. -/
theorem kernelToImage_blowupDotted (q₀ : ℕ) (h : IsBaseThreshold I q₀) (n c : ℕ) (hcn : c ≤ n)
    (M : ANCModule I n c) (i : ℕ) (q : ℤ) (hle : q - (c : ℤ) ≤ q)
    (x : (blowupModuleSituationOf I q₀ h n c hcn).HG M i q) :
    (blowupModuleSituationOf I q₀ h n c hcn).kernelToImage M i (q - c)
